Caching Dependencies in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how caching dependencies helps speed up workflows by avoiding repeated downloads.

🔹 Cache Action
GitHub provides a cache action to store:
Dependencies
Build outputs
Package files
Caches are reused across workflow runs.

🔹 Speeding Up Workflows
Caching helps:
Reduce pipeline execution time
Save compute resources
Improve developer productivity
Especially useful for large projects.

🔹 Cache Keys & Paths
Cache keys identify stored data
Paths define what to cache
Proper keys prevent cache conflicts
Good cache design improves efficiency.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Caching saves time.
 Keys control reuse.
 Efficient pipelines scale.
